        // - Otherwise (makeThisNonOwner==true or ownerBefore != address(this)), the call must revert and ownerAfter == ownerBefore_or_prior (i.e., owner did not change as a result).
        // We express owner-before-call as "ownerBefore" when makeThisNonOwner==false, and when makeThisNonOwner==true we forced the owner to 'other' and required it; so ownerBefore is the owner at start but when makeThisNonOwner==true we ensured owner changed to some other before the tested call and required it, hence ownerBefore is the value before any forced change — to capture the owner immediately before the tested call, we use c.owner() right after the optional transfer only in the reasoning below by relating branches.
